1.
What Types of Data We Collect
We may collect, process and hold a range of different Data about you, such as, but not limited to:
(a) personal particulars including name, date of birth,
age*
,
gender*
,
ethnicity*
, nationality;
(b) contact details including address, telephone number, mobile telephone number and/or email address;
(c) identification information including, details on your identification documentation such as Hong Kong Identity Card, passport, student card, staff card, driver’s licence, any other personal identifiers and biometric information including fingerprints and speech patterns;
(d) Data that you have shared with third party social media platform operators including account login name, profile picture and contact details;
(e) transactional information and payment details including credit card, debit card and other electronic banking, digital wallet or payment facility Data;
(f) account details or Data relating to the goods and/or services offered by us (the “
Services
”) or registered with us including the PIN, username, password, account numbers and service numbers;
(g) device specific information including browser type, IP address and/or domain name, connection data, hardware model, operating system, version, unique device identifier, serial numbers, setting configurations and software and mobile network configuration;
(h) information about how you use our Services such as network usage, how you use our network, your location when you are using our Services, as well as call recordings, chat history and any other form of communication;
(i) health and biometric information like your fingerprints and voice pattern that allows us to identify you for verification purpose as well as for the purposes of providing health and/or wellbeing related services to you;
(j) credit and service history to enable us to assess your eligibility for our offers of Services or to accommodate your request for transfer of Services or your account with us;
(k) blockchain data including wallet addresses, public keys and transaction information;
(l) website, mobile application and TV application usage data including user agent, domain name, referral URLs, location, phone contacts, browser and search history, statistics on page views, connection data, online activities and statistics, log data, device and software characteristics and configurations;
(m)
employment information*
including
education*
,
profession*
, salary range, current and previous employment details,
marital status*
,
family and household information/demographics*
;
(n) behavioural information including
hobbies*
, preferences and
leisure activities*
;
(o) all Data requested by applicable government authorities, courts, law enforcement or other authorities or regulatory bodies to enable us to comply with or in connection with any law, rule, regulation, judgment or court order (whether within or outside of Hong Kong); and
(p) any other Data as may be required by any members of PCCW and/or their respective contractors, sub-contractors, intermediaries, agents, business partners or representatives, brokers, underwriters from time to time and which is necessary for the provision of the Services.
In some instances, where required by the application Data Protection Laws, we may seek your consent to process those information bolded and marked * under Section III(1)(a), (m) and (n) of this Privacy Statement (collectively, the “
Special Categories of Data
”) so that we may further improve our Services and/or better tailor the type of information or content that we present to you. When possible, we will indicate during Data collection whether specific Data and/or Special Categories of Data (as the case may be) is mandatory or optional for us to enter into a contract with you or provide the Services to you.

3.
How we collect data
We collect your Data in several ways, including without limitation:
a. you directly (i) provide the Data by phone, customer service hotlines, online chat sessions or via email; (ii) complete a registration/application form/agreement and/or other relevant forms, documents or any other means (including but not limited to, if/where applicable, at or during our functions, events, campaigns, activities or the like); (iii) submit your Data through our websites, mobile or TV applications; (iv) contact us with a query or request; (v) provide during the ordinary course of the continuation of our business relationship with you; or (vi) provide the Data when we are legally required to do so;
b. third parties such as related entities, business partners, or other customers, or your representatives with appropriate consent from you;
c. publicly available sources;
d. our own records of how you use our Services;
e. your visits on our websites, or mobile or TV applications, including but not limited to the Tracking Data; and/or
f. your participation in surveys or marketing promotions organised by us or on our behalf, solely or in conjunction with Group Entities or any third parties.
Occasionally, you may need to provide Data about other individuals to us. If so, you should obtain those individuals’ authorisation and/or consent to such use, disclosure and transfer (or the extent to which such authorisation and/or consent was obtained). In case the other individuals are minor (the “
Minors
”), please ensure authorisation and/or consent from the Minors’ parents and/or legal guardians on such use, disclosure and transfer are obtained. You should also advise them where they can find a copy of this Privacy Statement and the relevant Personal Information Collection Statement and to contact us for further information as stated under the “How to Contact Us” section below.
IV. Use of Your Data

1.
How we use your data
We may collect, retain and use your Data for the following purposes:
a. Services Administration
(i) to verify your identity including but not limited to handling and processing your instructions, complaints and requests related to the above;
(ii) to verify your eligibility for our offers for Services, games and/or promotions or other events;
(iii) to process your application to subscribe to our Services and loyalty programmes operated by us and/or any members of the PCCW Group;
(iv) to provide, activate and/or renew Services, loyalty programmes operated by us or any members of the HKT Group;
(v) to process any payment instructions, direct debit facilities and/or credit facilities in relation to our supply of Services to you, including but not limited to handling and processing your instructions, complaints and request related to the above;
b. Optimisation, Personalisation and Marketing
(i) to provide you with rewards, promotional benefits, updates, offer and invitation to events;
(ii) to promote and market our Services to you through different means, including but not limited to the use of machine learning and/or artificial intelligence tools and/or models (collectively, the “
AI
”);
(iii) to perform research or analyses so that we may improve and optimise the Services and/or loyalty programmes that can be made available to you, such as through AI;
(iv) to conduct surveys and marketing, promotional, behavioural scoring for business operations, your needs and preferences and/or planning purposes, such as through the use of AI, and carry out behavioural, market and product analyses for profiling, generating statistical or actuarial reports (containing aggregated data that does not relate to any identified or identifiable individual), information management and database administration;
(v) to maintain, enhance and develop various products and service offerings through different means, including but not limited to the use of AI;
(vi) to distribute our publications and research materials as well as those of our business partners and counterparties;
(vii) to maintain and develop our systems and infrastructure, including testing and upgrading of these systems;
(viii) to carry out matching procedures, as defined under the applicable Data Protection Laws;
(ix) to carry out market and product analyses in order to generate statistical or actuarial reports (containing aggregated data that does not relate to any identified or identifiable individual);
(x) to develop financial services and products;
c. Legal and Administration
(i) to conduct credit checks and detect fraudulent activities in compliance with the Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorist Financing (Financial Institutions) Ordinance (Cap. 615 of the laws of Hong Kong) and in relation to other compliance purposes;
(ii) to enforce our contractual rights and statutory rights;
(iii) to comply with our obligations under the Broadcasting Ordinance (Cap.562) and our television programme service licence(s);
(iv) to evaluate your financial needs and insurance claims made by or against you, and to process claims involving you (including but not limited to making, defending, analysing, investigating, processing, assessing, determining, responding to, resolving or settling such claims); and
(v) to comply with applicable laws in or outside Hong Kong as may be required by applicable government authorities, courts, law enforcement, or regulatory or investigation bodies, in relation to the supply of Services and/or loyalty programmes to you, including to assist in the investigation, prevention, detection of crime or possible criminal activities.

2.
How We Share and Disclose Your Data
We have a legitimate interest in properly administering the Services. Our use of your Data may be necessary for the performance of the Services you have requested. Your Data will be held by one or more Group Entity and will be accessible by employees of such Group Entity consistent with the situations or for the purposes set out in this Privacy Statement or as otherwise indicated by prior notice to you or, where required, by obtaining your consent. In addition, in order to provide the Services you have requested, we may, to the extent permissible under applicable laws and regulations (including but not limited to the Data Protection Laws), disclose or make available your Data to organisations or parties outside of PCCW (which may be within or outside of Hong Kong) (collectively, “
Organisations
”) to use, disclose, process or retain for the purposes mentioned above and any other purposes indicated in the following paragraphs. Your Data is disclosed to these Organisations for the strict purpose of enabling us to administer and supply our Services to you.
Without prejudice to the aforesaid, to provide the Services you have requested, we may disclose your Data to the Organisations which provide the following support services to our businesses and operations, including without limitation:
(a) customer enquiries;
(b) courier, delivery, logistic and warehouse services;
(c) mailing operations;
(d) billing and debt-recovery functions;
(e) information technology services;
(f) installation, maintenance and repair services;
(g) marketing, advertising and telemarketing services;
(h) market research;
(i) customer usage and behavioural analysis;
(j) process management;
(k) after sale services;
(l) surveys;
(m) website usage analysis; and
(n) cloud storage services.
We take the required steps to ensure that these Organisations involved in these circumstances are bound by appropriate confidentiality and privacy obligations under the Data Protection Laws in relation to the protection of your Data and that they use your Data for the sole purpose of carrying out the services for which they have been engaged, and not for their own or other purposes (including direct marketing), unless subject to your consent.

In addition, we may disclose your data to:
(a) PCCW Group including our affiliates, overseas offices, assignees, transferees and representatives (including any actual or proposed participant, assignee or transferee of all or any part of our business or operations);
(b) Hong Kong Economic Journal Company Limited and Pacific Century Premium Developments Limited;
(c) HKT Group including their affiliates, overseas offices, assignees, transferees and representatives (including any actual or proposed participant, assignee or transferee of all or any part of their business or operations);
(d) your authorised representatives and/or your legal advisers when requested by you to do so;
(e) for the purposes of providing administrative, payment, collection, business, legal and/or operational support, to the following parties:
(i) credit-reporting and fraud-checking agencies;
(ii) financial institutions, charge or credit card issuing companies, credit providers, credit bureau, collection agencies or security agencies;
(iii) telecommunications network or broadcasting operators;
(iv) our affiliates, overseas offices, assignees, transferees and representatives;
(v) our professional advisers, including our accountants, auditors, lawyers and insurers;
(f) banks, hotels, insurance companies, insurance brokers, underwriters, billing agents and various business partners for reward redemption purposes and benefits applicable to members of the loyalty programmes operated by us and/or any members of the HKT Group, including without limitation for the purpose of registering members for loyalty programme related events;
(g) government and regulatory authorities and other organisations, as required or authorised by law;
(h) organisations who manage our business and corporate strategies, including those involved in a transfer or sale of all or part of our assets or business (including accounts and trade receivables) and those involved in managing our corporate risk and funding functions (e.g. securitisation);
(i) any proposed or actual participant, assignee or transferee of all or any part of the relevant member of our operations or business; and/or
(j) charities or non-profit organisations.
